config BR2_PACKAGE_TERMINAL
	bool "terminal (terminal emulator)"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC_TARGET_ARCH_SUPPORTS
	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_THREADS
	depends on !BR2_STATIC_LIBS
	select BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC
	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBXKBCOMMON
	select BR2_PACKAGE_VULKAN_LOADER
	select BR2_PACKAGE_WAYLAND
	help
	  The AOS terminal emulator: an awin + tgn window with a pty
	  behind it and its own escape-sequence parser, on the same
	  Wayland + Vulkan stack as the rest of the desktop.

	  This is what ade's Super+Return and Super+T spawn, which is
	  why ade selects it. With no terminal on the image there is no
	  way to reach a shell from the session at all.

	  It runs $SHELL, falling back to /bin/bash, and tells it
	  TERM=xterm-256color -- an entry ncurses installs by default,
	  so no terminfo needs adding for it.

	  Like notepad it draws with Vulkan, so the loader selected here
	  finds nothing unless an ICD is installed too. There is no one
	  symbol to depend on for that; the AOS defconfig turns on the
	  Intel, AMD, virtio and swrast Mesa drivers, and swrast is what
	  makes this work on a machine with no Vulkan hardware.

	  It needs no fonts on the image: tgn's built-in face is
	  proportional and a grid cannot use it, so the terminal
	  compiles in Liberation Mono of its own.

comment "terminal needs a toolchain w/ threads and dynamic libs"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_RUSTC_TARGET_ARCH_SUPPORTS
	depends on !BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_THREADS || BR2_STATIC_LIBS
